//==================================================
// SEP VCS coverage exclusions -- structural ties in sep_crypto and the eFuse
// command path: ABR, OTBN, AES, HMAC and KMAC wrappers and their key regblocks,
// the KV shim, the crypto AXI interconnect, TRNG (entropy_source, DRBG, EDN
// adapters), key_manager (xbar, mailbox, KPV, CPU, scramblers, OTP error slave),
// the eFuse wrapper and controller, sep_lifecycle_ctrl, the eFuse ID converter,
// sep_crypto top, and the eFuse interface shim of the reference integration.
// Format Version: 2
// ExclMode: default
//
// Scope: the cocotb VCS elaboration of sep_uvm_top, target `default`, applied on
// top of the other cov/config/vcs exclusion files and sep_cov_scope.hier. Most
// blocks are INSTANCE-scoped TOGGLE exclusions. One block is MODULE-scoped
// (gf_muladd, TOGGLE) and one block is a BLOCK exclusion in
// efuse_shadow_reg_access_control. Only TT-owned instances carry entries; no
// entry is written inside a third-party module.
//
// Honesty rule 1: every block waives a bit or a statement that a literal tie, an
// elaborated parameter, a localparam or a width cast in SEP RTL fixes for every
// legal input. A constant that the reference integration drives into a SEP input
// port is not an RTL tie and is not in this file. The eFuse interface shim block
// waives shim input bits that SEP RTL literals drive through the integration
// wiring. A bit that a test, a fault, an error response, an illegal CSR value, an
// integrator, JTAG or a second master can move is a test gap and is not in this
// file.
// Honesty rule 2: the file passes urg -excl_strict, which refuses to
// exclude any object some leaf already covered. A strict-mode refusal means the
// reason is wrong; delete the entry, do not weaken the check.
// Every ANNOTATION cites the tie as file:line.
//==================================================

